[{"input":"# Lecture 9 – Cybersecurity and Cryptography \n\n## Learning Objectives \n\nAt the end of this chapter, students should be able to: \n\n- Explain why cybersecurity is important. \n\n- Understand the concepts of assets, threats, vulnerabilities, and risks. \n\n- Distinguish between authentication and authorization. \n\n- Explain the basic principles of cryptography. \n\n- Understand encryption, hashing, and digital signatures. \n\n- Recognize common cyberattacks. \n\n- Understand social engineering and phishing. \n\n- Apply basic cybersecurity best practices. ","output":"","result":"# Lecture 9 – Cybersecurity and Cryptography \n\n## Learning Objectives \n\nAt the end of this chapter, students should be able to: \n\n- Explain why cybersecurity is important. \n\n- Understand the concepts of assets, threats, vulnerabilities, and risks. \n\n- Distinguish between authentication and authorization. \n\n- Explain the basic principles of cryptography. \n\n- Understand encryption, hashing, and digital signatures. \n\n- Recognize common cyberattacks. \n\n- Understand social engineering and phishing. \n\n- Apply basic cybersecurity best practices. ","resultHTML":"<section data-type=\"chapter\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture09-c3494-lecture-9-cybersecurity-and-cryptography\">\n<h1>Lecture 9 – Cybersecurity and Cryptography</h1>\n<section data-type=\"sect1\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture09-c3494-learning-objectives\">\n<h1>Learning Objectives</h1>\n<p>At the end of this chapter, students should be able to:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Explain why cybersecurity is important.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Understand the concepts of assets, threats, vulnerabilities, and risks.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Distinguish between authentication and authorization.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Explain the basic principles of cryptography.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Understand encryption, hashing, and digital signatures.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Recognize common cyberattacks.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Understand social engineering and phishing.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Apply basic cybersecurity best practices.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</section>\n</section>\n","hidden":true,"type":"markdown","translations":{"Dutch":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"5576ffc986e7b49ea9e9bd933a01cf2a5018ff467e46fff52f6457fecf34fc02","markdown":"# Les 9 – Cyberbeveiliging en Cryptografie \n\n## Leerdoelen \n\nAan het einde van dit hoofdstuk moeten studenten in staat zijn om: \n\n- Uit te leggen waarom cyberbeveiliging belangrijk is. \n\n- De concepten van bedrijfsmiddelen, bedreigingen, kwetsbaarheden en risico's te begrijpen. \n\n- Een onderscheid te maken tussen authenticatie en autorisatie. \n\n- De basisprincipes van cryptografie uit te leggen. \n\n- Encryptie, hashing en digitale handtekeningen te begrijpen. \n\n- Veelvoorkomende cyberaanvallen te herkennen. \n\n- Social engineering en phishing te begrijpen. \n\n- Basisprincipes van cyberbeveiliging toe te passen. \n"},"French":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"5576ffc986e7b49ea9e9bd933a01cf2a5018ff467e46fff52f6457fecf34fc02","markdown":"# Cours 9 – Cybersécurité et Cryptographie \n\n## Objectifs d'apprentissage \n\nÀ la fin de ce chapitre, les étudiants devraient être capables de : \n\n- Expliquer pourquoi la cybersécurité est importante. \n\n- Comprendre les concepts d'actifs, de menaces, de vulnérabilités et de risques. \n\n- Distinguer entre authentification et autorisation. \n\n- Expliquer les principes de base de la cryptographie. \n\n- Comprendre le chiffrement, le hachage et les signatures numériques. \n\n- Reconnaître les cyberattaques courantes. \n\n- Comprendre l'ingénierie sociale et l'hameçonnage. \n\n- Appliquer les bonnes pratiques de base en cybersécurité. "}},"translationSource":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"5576ffc986e7b49ea9e9bd933a01cf2a5018ff467e46fff52f6457fecf34fc02","language":"English"}},{"input":"## Introduction \n\nComputers and networks have transformed modern society. \n\nWe now use digital systems for: \n\n- Banking \n\n- Shopping \n\n- Healthcare \n\n- Education \n\n- Communication \n\n- Government services \n\nHowever, increased connectivity also creates new risks. \n\nExamples include: \n\n- Data theft \n\n- Identity theft \n\n- Malware infections \n\n- Financial fraud \n\n- Privacy violations \n\nCybersecurity aims to reduce these risks and protect digital systems. ","output":"","result":"## Introduction \n\nComputers and networks have transformed modern society. \n\nWe now use digital systems for: \n\n- Banking \n\n- Shopping \n\n- Healthcare \n\n- Education \n\n- Communication \n\n- Government services \n\nHowever, increased connectivity also creates new risks. \n\nExamples include: \n\n- Data theft \n\n- Identity theft \n\n- Malware infections \n\n- Financial fraud \n\n- Privacy violations \n\nCybersecurity aims to reduce these risks and protect digital systems. ","resultHTML":"<section data-type=\"sect1\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture09-c3496-introduction\">\n<h1>Introduction</h1>\n<p>Computers and networks have transformed modern society.</p>\n<p>We now use digital systems for:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Banking</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Shopping</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Healthcare</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Education</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Communication</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Government services</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>However, increased connectivity also creates new risks.</p>\n<p>Examples include:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Data theft</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Identity theft</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Malware infections</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Financial fraud</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Privacy violations</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Cybersecurity aims to reduce these risks and protect digital systems.</p>\n</section>\n","hidden":true,"type":"markdown","translations":{"Dutch":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"b60f4f937eb5cd53e9f853420b5bab364cd974efa0d784fd1bd500f473f5db8d","markdown":"## Inleiding \n\nComputers en netwerken hebben de moderne samenleving veranderd. \n\nWe gebruiken nu digitale systemen voor: \n\n- Bankzaken \n\n- Winkelen \n\n- Gezondheidszorg \n\n- Onderwijs \n\n- Communicatie \n\n- Overheidsdiensten \n\nEchter, toegenomen connectiviteit creëert ook nieuwe risico's. \n\nVoorbeelden zijn: \n\n- Datadiefstal \n\n- Identiteitsdiefstal \n\n- Malware-infecties \n\n- Financiële fraude \n\n- Schendingen van privacy \n\nCybersecurity heeft als doel deze risico's te verminderen en digitale systemen te beschermen. "},"French":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"b60f4f937eb5cd53e9f853420b5bab364cd974efa0d784fd1bd500f473f5db8d","markdown":"## Introduction \n\nLes ordinateurs et les réseaux ont transformé la société moderne. \n\nNous utilisons désormais des systèmes numériques pour : \n\n- La banque \n\n- Les achats \n\n- Les soins de santé \n\n- L'éducation \n\n- La communication \n\n- Les services publics \n\nCependant, une connectivité accrue crée également de nouveaux risques. \n\nEn voici des exemples : \n\n- Le vol de données \n\n- L'usurpation d'identité \n\n- Les infections par logiciels malveillants \n\n- La fraude financière \n\n- Les atteintes à la vie privée \n\nLa cybersécurité vise à réduire ces risques et à protéger les systèmes numériques. \n"}},"translationSource":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"b60f4f937eb5cd53e9f853420b5bab364cd974efa0d784fd1bd500f473f5db8d","language":"English"}},{"input":"## What Is Cybersecurity? \n\nCybersecurity is the practice of protecting: \n\n- Computers \n\n- Networks \n\n- Software \n\n- Data \n\n- Digital services \n\nfrom unauthorized access, damage, disruption, or theft. \n\n \n\n### Why Cybersecurity Matters \n\nConsider what would happen if a malicious individual gained access to: \n\n- Your email account \n\n- Your online banking account \n\n- University records \n\n- Medical information \n\nThe consequences could be significant. \n\n \n\n### Everyday Examples \n\nCybersecurity affects: \n\n- Smartphones \n\n- Laptops \n\n- Social media accounts \n\n- Online shopping \n\n- Cloud services \n\nCybersecurity is therefore a concern for everyone, not just IT professionals. ","output":"","result":"## What Is Cybersecurity? \n\nCybersecurity is the practice of protecting: \n\n- Computers \n\n- Networks \n\n- Software \n\n- Data \n\n- Digital services \n\nfrom unauthorized access, damage, disruption, or theft. \n\n \n\n### Why Cybersecurity Matters \n\nConsider what would happen if a malicious individual gained access to: \n\n- Your email account \n\n- Your online banking account \n\n- University records \n\n- Medical information \n\nThe consequences could be significant. \n\n \n\n### Everyday Examples \n\nCybersecurity affects: \n\n- Smartphones \n\n- Laptops \n\n- Social media accounts \n\n- Online shopping \n\n- Cloud services \n\nCybersecurity is therefore a concern for everyone, not just IT professionals. ","resultHTML":"<section data-type=\"sect1\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture09-c3497-what-is-cybersecurity\">\n<h1>What Is Cybersecurity?</h1>\n<p>Cybersecurity is the practice of protecting:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Computers</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Networks</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Software</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Data</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Digital services</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>from unauthorized access, damage, disruption, or theft.</p>\n<section data-type=\"sect2\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture09-c3497-why-cybersecurity-matters\">\n<h1>Why Cybersecurity Matters</h1>\n<p>Consider what would happen if a malicious individual gained access to:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Your email account</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Your online banking account</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>University records</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Medical information</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The consequences could be significant.</p>\n</section>\n<section data-type=\"sect2\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture09-c3497-everyday-examples\">\n<h1>Everyday Examples</h1>\n<p>Cybersecurity affects:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Smartphones</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Laptops</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Social media accounts</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Online shopping</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Cloud services</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Cybersecurity is therefore a concern for everyone, not just IT professionals.</p>\n</section>\n</section>\n","hidden":true,"type":"markdown","translations":{"Dutch":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"737b9eb091d147e90873f82fbb4ffac48248b66f00fa762836bd1547ae6f0774","markdown":"## Wat Is Cyberbeveiliging? \n\nCyberbeveiliging is de praktijk van het beschermen van: \n\n- Computers \n\n- Netwerken \n\n- Software \n\n- Data \n\n- Digitale diensten \n\ntegen ongeoorloofde toegang, schade, verstoring of diefstal. \n\n \n\n### Waarom Cyberbeveiliging Belangrijk Is \n\nBedenk wat er zou gebeuren als een kwaadwillende persoon toegang zou krijgen tot: \n\n- Uw e-mailaccount \n\n- Uw online bankrekening \n\n- Universitaire gegevens \n\n- Medische informatie \n\nDe gevolgen zouden aanzienlijk kunnen zijn. \n\n \n\n### Alledaagse Voorbeelden \n\nCyberbeveiliging heeft invloed op: \n\n- Smartphones \n\n- Laptops \n\n- Sociale-mediaccounts \n\n- Online winkelen \n\n- Cloudservices \n\nCyberbeveiliging is daarom een zorg voor iedereen, niet alleen voor IT-professionals. "},"French":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"737b9eb091d147e90873f82fbb4ffac48248b66f00fa762836bd1547ae6f0774","markdown":"## Qu'est-ce que la cybersécurité ? \n\nLa cybersécurité est la pratique consistant à protéger : \n\n- Les ordinateurs \n\n- Les réseaux \n\n- Les logiciels \n\n- Les données \n\n- Les services numériques \n\ncontre l'accès non autorisé, les dommages, les perturbations ou le vol. \n\n \n\n### Pourquoi la cybersécurité est-elle importante \n\nImaginez ce qui se passerait si une personne malveillante accédait à : \n\n- Votre compte de messagerie \n\n- Votre compte bancaire en ligne \n\n- Les dossiers universitaires \n\n- Les informations médicales \n\nLes conséquences pourraient être importantes. \n\n \n\n### Exemples du quotidien \n\nLa cybersécurité concerne : \n\n- Les smartphones \n\n- Les ordinateurs portables \n\n- Les comptes de réseaux sociaux \n\n- Les achats en ligne \n\n- Les services infonuagiques \n\nLa cybersécurité est donc l'affaire de tous, pas seulement des professionnels de l'informatique. "}},"translationSource":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"737b9eb091d147e90873f82fbb4ffac48248b66f00fa762836bd1547ae6f0774","language":"English"}},{"input":"## Assets, Threats, Vulnerabilities, and Risks \n\nSecurity professionals often use four important concepts. \n\n \n\n### Asset \n\nAn asset is something valuable that needs protection. \n\nExamples: \n\n- Personal data \n\n- Documents \n\n- Passwords \n\n- Financial records \n\n- Company databases \n\n \n\n### Threat \n\nA threat is anything capable of causing harm. \n\nExamples: \n\n- Hackers \n\n- Malware \n\n- Dishonest employees \n\n- Hardware failures \n\n- Natural disasters \n\n \n\n### Vulnerability \n\nA vulnerability is a weakness that can be exploited. \n\nExamples: \n\n- Weak passwords \n\n- Outdated software \n\n- Misconfigured systems \n\n- Unsecured Wi-Fi \n\n \n\n### Risk \n\nRisk is the possibility that a threat will exploit a vulnerability and harm an asset. \n\n \n\n### Example\n\n\n```text\n     Asset: \n         Online Banking Account      \n     Threat: \n         Cybercriminal \n     Vulnerability: \n         Weak Password \n     Risk: \n         Unauthorized Access \n```","output":"","result":"## Assets, Threats, Vulnerabilities, and Risks \n\nSecurity professionals often use four important concepts. \n\n \n\n### Asset \n\nAn asset is something valuable that needs protection. \n\nExamples: \n\n- Personal data \n\n- Documents \n\n- Passwords \n\n- Financial records \n\n- Company databases \n\n \n\n### Threat \n\nA threat is anything capable of causing harm. \n\nExamples: \n\n- Hackers \n\n- Malware \n\n- Dishonest employees \n\n- Hardware failures \n\n- Natural disasters \n\n \n\n### Vulnerability \n\nA vulnerability is a weakness that can be exploited. \n\nExamples: \n\n- Weak passwords \n\n- Outdated software \n\n- Misconfigured systems \n\n- Unsecured Wi-Fi \n\n \n\n### Risk \n\nRisk is the possibility that a threat will exploit a vulnerability and harm an asset. \n\n \n\n### Example\n\n\n```text\n     Asset: \n         Online Banking Account      \n     Threat: \n         Cybercriminal \n     Vulnerability: \n         Weak Password \n     Risk: \n         Unauthorized Access \n```","resultHTML":"<section data-type=\"sect1\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture09-c3498-assets-threats-vulnerabilities-and-risks\">\n<h1>Assets, Threats, Vulnerabilities, and Risks</h1>\n<p>Security professionals often use four important concepts.</p>\n<section data-type=\"sect2\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture09-c3498-asset\">\n<h1>Asset</h1>\n<p>An asset is something valuable that needs protection.</p>\n<p>Examples:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Personal data</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Documents</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Passwords</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Financial records</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Company databases</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</section>\n<section data-type=\"sect2\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture09-c3498-threat\">\n<h1>Threat</h1>\n<p>A threat is anything capable of causing harm.</p>\n<p>Examples:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Hackers</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Malware</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Dishonest employees</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Hardware failures</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Natural disasters</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</section>\n<section data-type=\"sect2\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture09-c3498-vulnerability\">\n<h1>Vulnerability</h1>\n<p>A vulnerability is a weakness that can be exploited.</p>\n<p>Examples:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Weak passwords</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Outdated software</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Misconfigured systems</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Unsecured Wi-Fi</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</section>\n<section data-type=\"sect2\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture09-c3498-risk\">\n<h1>Risk</h1>\n<p>Risk is the possibility that a threat will exploit a vulnerability and harm an asset.</p>\n</section>\n<section data-type=\"sect2\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture09-c3498-example\">\n<h1>Example</h1>\n<pre data-type=\"program-listing\" data-code-language=\"text\">     Asset: \n         Online Banking Account      \n     Threat: \n         Cybercriminal \n     Vulnerability: \n         Weak Password \n     Risk: \n         Unauthorized Access </pre>\n</section>\n</section>\n","hidden":true,"type":"markdown","translations":{"Dutch":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"c11785b03d516e4cd15622e3e65f6a105f5b143494aeb2d1198873da769de045","markdown":"## Assets, Bedreigingen, Kwetsbaarheden en Risico's \n\nBeveiligingsprofessionals gebruiken vaak vier belangrijke begrippen. \n\n \n\n### Asset \n\nEen asset is iets waardevols dat bescherming nodig heeft. \n\nVoorbeelden: \n\n- Persoonlijke gegevens \n\n- Documenten \n\n- Wachtwoorden \n\n- Financiële gegevens \n\n- Bedrijfsdatabases \n\n \n\n### Bedreiging \n\nEen bedreiging is alles wat schade kan veroorzaken. \n\nVoorbeelden: \n\n- Hackers \n\n- Malware \n\n- Oneerlijke werknemers \n\n- Hardwarestoringen \n\n- Natuurrampen \n\n \n\n### Kwetsbaarheid \n\nEen kwetsbaarheid is een zwakte die kan worden misbruikt. \n\nVoorbeelden: \n\n- Zwakke wachtwoorden \n\n- Verouderde software \n\n- Verkeerd geconfigureerde systemen \n\n- Onbeveiligde wifi \n\n \n\n### Risico \n\nRisico is de kans dat een bedreiging een kwetsbaarheid misbruikt en een asset schaadt. \n\n \n\n### Voorbeeld\n\n\n```text\n     Asset: \n         Online Banking Account      \n     Threat: \n         Cybercriminal \n     Vulnerability: \n         Weak Password \n     Risk: \n         Unauthorized Access \n```"},"French":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"c11785b03d516e4cd15622e3e65f6a105f5b143494aeb2d1198873da769de045","markdown":"## Actifs, menaces, vulnérabilités et risques \n\nLes professionnels de la sécurité utilisent souvent quatre concepts importants. \n\n \n\n### Actif \n\nUn actif est quelque chose de précieux qui doit être protégé. \n\nExemples : \n\n- Données personnelles \n\n- Documents \n\n- Mots de passe \n\n- Dossiers financiers \n\n- Bases de données de l'entreprise \n\n \n\n### Menace \n\nUne menace est tout ce qui est capable de causer un préjudice. \n\nExemples : \n\n- Pirates informatiques \n\n- Logiciels malveillants \n\n- Employés malhonnêtes \n\n- Pannes matérielles \n\n- Catastrophes naturelles \n\n \n\n### Vulnérabilité \n\nUne vulnérabilité est une faiblesse qui peut être exploitée. \n\nExemples : \n\n- Mots de passe faibles \n\n- Logiciels obsolètes \n\n- Systèmes mal configurés \n\n- Wi-Fi non sécurisé \n\n \n\n### Risque \n\nLe risque est la possibilité qu'une menace exploite une vulnérabilité et nuise à un actif. \n\n \n\n### Exemple\n\n\n```text\n     Asset: \n         Online Banking Account      \n     Threat: \n         Cybercriminal \n     Vulnerability: \n         Weak Password \n     Risk: \n         Unauthorized Access \n```"}},"translationSource":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"c11785b03d516e4cd15622e3e65f6a105f5b143494aeb2d1198873da769de045","language":"English"}},{"input":"## Security Goals \n\nCybersecurity is often organized around three primary goals. \n\n \n\n### Confidentiality \n\nProtect information from unauthorized access. \n\n \n\nExamples \n\n- Medical records \n\n- Examination results \n\n- Financial information \n\nOnly authorized individuals should have access. \n\n \n\n### Integrity \n\nProtect information from unauthorized modification. \n\n \n\nExample \n\nA student's grade should not be altered by unauthorized users. \n\nThe information must remain accurate and trustworthy. \n\n \n\n### Availability \n\nEnsure systems remain accessible when needed. \n\n \n\nExample \n\nAn online learning platform should remain available during exam periods. \n\n \n\n### CIA Triad \n\nThe three goals are commonly known as: \n\n```texy\n     Confidentiality \n     Integrity \n     Availability \n```\n\nor simply: \n\n```text\n     CIA\n```","output":"","result":"## Security Goals \n\nCybersecurity is often organized around three primary goals. \n\n \n\n### Confidentiality \n\nProtect information from unauthorized access. \n\n \n\nExamples \n\n- Medical records \n\n- Examination results \n\n- Financial information \n\nOnly authorized individuals should have access. \n\n \n\n### Integrity \n\nProtect information from unauthorized modification. \n\n \n\nExample \n\nA student's grade should not be altered by unauthorized users. \n\nThe information must remain accurate and trustworthy. \n\n \n\n### Availability \n\nEnsure systems remain accessible when needed. \n\n \n\nExample \n\nAn online learning platform should remain available during exam periods. \n\n \n\n### CIA Triad \n\nThe three goals are commonly known as: \n\n```texy\n     Confidentiality \n     Integrity \n     Availability \n```\n\nor simply: \n\n```text\n     CIA\n```","resultHTML":"<section data-type=\"sect1\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture09-c3499-security-goals\">\n<h1>Security Goals</h1>\n<p>Cybersecurity is often organized around three primary goals.</p>\n<section data-type=\"sect2\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture09-c3499-confidentiality\">\n<h1>Confidentiality</h1>\n<p>Protect information from unauthorized access.</p>\n<p>Examples</p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Medical records</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Examination results</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Financial information</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Only authorized individuals should have access.</p>\n</section>\n<section data-type=\"sect2\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture09-c3499-integrity\">\n<h1>Integrity</h1>\n<p>Protect information from unauthorized modification.</p>\n<p>Example</p>\n<p>A student’s grade should not be altered by unauthorized users.</p>\n<p>The information must remain accurate and trustworthy.</p>\n</section>\n<section data-type=\"sect2\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture09-c3499-availability\">\n<h1>Availability</h1>\n<p>Ensure systems remain accessible when needed.</p>\n<p>Example</p>\n<p>An online learning platform should remain available during exam periods.</p>\n</section>\n<section data-type=\"sect2\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture09-c3499-cia-triad\">\n<h1>CIA Triad</h1>\n<p>The three goals are commonly known as:</p>\n<pre data-type=\"program-listing\" data-code-language=\"texy\">     Confidentiality \n     Integrity \n     Availability </pre>\n<p>or simply:</p>\n<pre data-type=\"program-listing\" data-code-language=\"text\">     CIA</pre>\n</section>\n</section>\n","hidden":true,"type":"markdown","translations":{"Dutch":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"0383788b52dba7412f26d151ec801df2440ebd2efc06327b15d51397285e4724","markdown":"## Beveiligingsdoelen\n\nCyberbeveiliging wordt vaak georganiseerd rond drie primaire doelen.\n\n\n\n### Vertrouwelijkheid\n\nBescherm informatie tegen ongeautoriseerde toegang.\n\n\n\nVoorbeelden\n\n- Medische dossiers\n\n- Examenresultaten\n\n- Financiële informatie\n\nAlleen geautoriseerde personen zouden toegang moeten hebben.\n\n\n\n### Integriteit\n\nBescherm informatie tegen ongeautoriseerde wijziging.\n\n\n\nVoorbeeld\n\nHet cijfer van een student mag niet worden gewijzigd door ongeautoriseerde gebruikers.\n\nDe informatie moet accuraat en betrouwbaar blijven.\n\n\n\n### Beschikbaarheid\n\nZorg ervoor dat systemen toegankelijk blijven wanneer nodig.\n\n\n\nVoorbeeld\n\nEen online leerplatform moet beschikbaar blijven tijdens examenperiodes.\n\n\n\n### CIA-triade\n\nDe drie doelen staan algemeen bekend als:\n\n```texy\n     Confidentiality \n     Integrity \n     Availability \n```\n\nof eenvoudigweg:\n\n```text\n     CIA\n```"},"French":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"0383788b52dba7412f26d151ec801df2440ebd2efc06327b15d51397285e4724","markdown":"## Objectifs de sécurité\n\nLa cybersécurité est souvent organisée autour de trois objectifs principaux.\n\n\n\n### Confidentialité\n\nProtéger les informations contre tout accès non autorisé.\n\n\n\nExemples\n\n- Dossiers médicaux\n\n- Résultats d'examens\n\n- Informations financières\n\nSeules les personnes autorisées devraient y avoir accès.\n\n\n\n### Intégrité\n\nProtéger les informations contre toute modification non autorisée.\n\n\n\nExemple\n\nLa note d'un étudiant ne devrait pas être modifiée par des utilisateurs non autorisés.\n\nL'information doit rester exacte et fiable.\n\n\n\n### Disponibilité\n\nGarantir que les systèmes restent accessibles en cas de besoin.\n\n\n\nExemple\n\nUne plateforme d'apprentissage en ligne devrait rester disponible pendant les périodes d'examen.\n\n\n\n### Triade CIA\n\nCes trois objectifs sont communément connus sous le nom de :\n\n```texy\n     Confidentiality \n     Integrity \n     Availability \n```\n\nou simplement :\n\n```text\n     CIA\n```"}},"translationSource":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"0383788b52dba7412f26d151ec801df2440ebd2efc06327b15d51397285e4724","language":"English"}},{"input":"## Authentication and Authorization \n\nThese concepts are often confused. \n\n \n\n### Authentication \n\nAuthentication answers: \n\nWho are you? \n\nIt verifies identity. \n\n \n\nExamples \n\n- Password \n\n- Smart card \n\n- Fingerprint \n\n- Facial recognition \n\n \n\n### Authorization \n\nAuthorization answers: \n\nWhat are you allowed to do? \n\n \n\nExample \n\nTwo employees may successfully log in. \n\nHowever: \n\n- One can view grades. \n\n- One can modify grades. \n\nThe difference is authorization. \n\n \n\n### Summary \n\n```text\n     Authentication = Identity \n     Authorization = Permissions \n```\n ","output":"","result":"## Authentication and Authorization \n\nThese concepts are often confused. \n\n \n\n### Authentication \n\nAuthentication answers: \n\nWho are you? \n\nIt verifies identity. \n\n \n\nExamples \n\n- Password \n\n- Smart card \n\n- Fingerprint \n\n- Facial recognition \n\n \n\n### Authorization \n\nAuthorization answers: \n\nWhat are you allowed to do? \n\n \n\nExample \n\nTwo employees may successfully log in. \n\nHowever: \n\n- One can view grades. \n\n- One can modify grades. \n\nThe difference is authorization. \n\n \n\n### Summary \n\n```text\n     Authentication = Identity \n     Authorization = Permissions \n```\n ","resultHTML":"<section data-type=\"sect1\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture09-c3500-authentication-and-authorization\">\n<h1>Authentication and Authorization</h1>\n<p>These concepts are often confused.</p>\n<section data-type=\"sect2\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture09-c3500-authentication\">\n<h1>Authentication</h1>\n<p>Authentication answers:</p>\n<p>Who are you?</p>\n<p>It verifies identity.</p>\n<p>Examples</p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Password</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Smart card</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Fingerprint</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Facial recognition</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</section>\n<section data-type=\"sect2\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture09-c3500-authorization\">\n<h1>Authorization</h1>\n<p>Authorization answers:</p>\n<p>What are you allowed to do?</p>\n<p>Example</p>\n<p>Two employees may successfully log in.</p>\n<p>However:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>One can view grades.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>One can modify grades.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The difference is authorization.</p>\n</section>\n<section data-type=\"sect2\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture09-c3500-summary\">\n<h1>Summary</h1>\n<pre data-type=\"program-listing\" data-code-language=\"text\">     Authentication = Identity \n     Authorization = Permissions </pre>\n</section>\n</section>\n","hidden":true,"type":"markdown","translations":{"Dutch":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"284286a1407a2d02d8d29fa290eb48351f08cdab9ea52d807f70ed46e372336f","markdown":"## Authenticatie en Autorisatie \n\nDeze begrippen worden vaak door elkaar gehaald. \n\n \n\n### Authenticatie \n\nAuthenticatie beantwoordt: \n\nWie ben je? \n\nHet verifieert de identiteit. \n\n \n\nVoorbeelden \n\n- Wachtwoord \n\n- Smartcard \n\n- Vingerafdruk \n\n- Gezichtsherkenning \n\n \n\n### Autorisatie \n\nAutorisatie beantwoordt: \n\nWat mag je doen? \n\n \n\nVoorbeeld \n\nTwee werknemers kunnen succesvol inloggen. \n\nEchter: \n\n- De ene kan cijfers bekijken. \n\n- De andere kan cijfers wijzigen. \n\nHet verschil is autorisatie. \n\n \n\n### Samenvatting \n\n```text\n     Authentication = Identity \n     Authorization = Permissions \n```"},"French":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"284286a1407a2d02d8d29fa290eb48351f08cdab9ea52d807f70ed46e372336f","markdown":"## Authentification et autorisation \n\nCes concepts sont souvent confondus. \n\n \n\n### Authentification \n\nL'authentification répond à : \n\nQui êtes-vous ? \n\nElle vérifie l'identité. \n\n \n\nExemples \n\n- Mot de passe \n\n- Carte à puce \n\n- Empreinte digitale \n\n- Reconnaissance faciale \n\n \n\n### Autorisation \n\nL'autorisation répond à : \n\nQu'avez-vous le droit de faire ? \n\n \n\nExemple \n\nDeux employés peuvent se connecter avec succès. \n\nCependant : \n\n- L'un peut consulter les notes. \n\n- L'un peut modifier les notes. \n\nLa différence réside dans l'autorisation. \n\n \n\n### Résumé \n\n```text\n     Authentication = Identity \n     Authorization = Permissions \n```"}},"translationSource":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"284286a1407a2d02d8d29fa290eb48351f08cdab9ea52d807f70ed46e372336f","language":"English"}},{"input":"## Passwords \n\nPasswords remain one of the most common security mechanisms. \n\n \n\n### Weak Password Example \n\n```text\n     123456 \n```\n\nProblems: \n\n- Predictable \n\n- Easily guessed \n\n \n\n### Strong Password Example \n\n```text\n     P7f!xQ2@M8k# \n```\n\nCharacteristics: \n\n- Long \n\n- Random \n\n- Difficult to predict \n\n \n\n### Best Practices \n\nUse: \n\n- Unique passwords \n\n- Password managers \n\n- Long passphrases \n\nAvoid: \n\n- Reusing passwords \n\n- Sharing passwords ","output":"","result":"## Passwords \n\nPasswords remain one of the most common security mechanisms. \n\n \n\n### Weak Password Example \n\n```text\n     123456 \n```\n\nProblems: \n\n- Predictable \n\n- Easily guessed \n\n \n\n### Strong Password Example \n\n```text\n     P7f!xQ2@M8k# \n```\n\nCharacteristics: \n\n- Long \n\n- Random \n\n- Difficult to predict \n\n \n\n### Best Practices \n\nUse: \n\n- Unique passwords \n\n- Password managers \n\n- Long passphrases \n\nAvoid: \n\n- Reusing passwords \n\n- Sharing passwords ","resultHTML":"<section data-type=\"sect1\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture09-c3501-passwords\">\n<h1>Passwords</h1>\n<p>Passwords remain one of the most common security mechanisms.</p>\n<section data-type=\"sect2\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture09-c3501-weak-password-example\">\n<h1>Weak Password Example</h1>\n<pre data-type=\"program-listing\" data-code-language=\"text\">     123456 </pre>\n<p>Problems:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Predictable</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Easily guessed</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</section>\n<section data-type=\"sect2\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture09-c3501-strong-password-example\">\n<h1>Strong Password Example</h1>\n<pre data-type=\"program-listing\" data-code-language=\"text\">     P7f!xQ2@M8k# </pre>\n<p>Characteristics:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Long</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Random</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Difficult to predict</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</section>\n<section data-type=\"sect2\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture09-c3501-best-practices\">\n<h1>Best Practices</h1>\n<p>Use:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Unique passwords</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Password managers</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Long passphrases</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Avoid:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Reusing passwords</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Sharing passwords</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</section>\n</section>\n","hidden":true,"type":"markdown","translations":{"Dutch":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"4a3fd5f38d023ff915a8fe4c9c0bfe2019e1aa355ed2cb77f9ba52434db2977f","markdown":"## Wachtwoorden \n\nWachtwoorden blijven een van de meest gebruikte beveiligingsmechanismen. \n\n \n\n### Voorbeeld van een zwak wachtwoord \n\n```text\n     123456 \n```\n\nProblemen: \n\n- Voorspelbaar \n\n- Gemakkelijk te raden \n\n \n\n### Voorbeeld van een sterk wachtwoord \n\n```text\n     P7f!xQ2@M8k# \n```\n\nKenmerken: \n\n- Lang \n\n- Willekeurig \n\n- Moeilijk te voorspellen \n\n \n\n### Beste praktijken \n\nGebruik: \n\n- Unieke wachtwoorden \n\n- Wachtwoordmanagers \n\n- Lange wachtwoordzinnen \n\nVermijd: \n\n- Wachtwoorden hergebruiken \n\n- Wachtwoorden delen "},"French":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"4a3fd5f38d023ff915a8fe4c9c0bfe2019e1aa355ed2cb77f9ba52434db2977f","markdown":"## Mots de passe \n\nLes mots de passe restent l'un des mécanismes de sécurité les plus courants. \n\n \n\n### Exemple de mot de passe faible \n\n```text\n     123456 \n```\n\nProblèmes : \n\n- Prévisible \n\n- Facile à deviner \n\n \n\n### Exemple de mot de passe fort \n\n```text\n     P7f!xQ2@M8k# \n```\n\nCaractéristiques : \n\n- Long \n\n- Aléatoire \n\n- Difficile à prévoir \n\n \n\n### Meilleures pratiques \n\nÀ utiliser : \n\n- Mots de passe uniques \n\n- Gestionnaires de mots de passe \n\n- Phrases de passe longues \n\nÀ éviter : \n\n- Réutiliser les mots de passe \n\n- Partager les mots de passe "}},"translationSource":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"4a3fd5f38d023ff915a8fe4c9c0bfe2019e1aa355ed2cb77f9ba52434db2977f","language":"English"}},{"input":"## Multi-Factor Authentication (MFA) \n\nPasswords alone are often insufficient. \n\nMulti-Factor Authentication adds additional verification steps. \n\n \n\n### Authentication Factors \n\n#### Something You Know \n\nExample: \n\n```text\n     Password \n```\n \n\n#### Something You Have \n\nExample: \n\n```text\n     Smartphone \n     Security Key \n```\n\n#### Something You Are \n\nExample: \n\n```texy\n     Fingerprint \n\n     Face Recognition \n```\n \n\n### Example \n\nOnline banking commonly requires: \n\n```text\n     Password \n     + \n     Verification Code \n```\n\nEven if a password is stolen, the account remains better protected. ","output":"","result":"## Multi-Factor Authentication (MFA) \n\nPasswords alone are often insufficient. \n\nMulti-Factor Authentication adds additional verification steps. \n\n \n\n### Authentication Factors \n\n#### Something You Know \n\nExample: \n\n```text\n     Password \n```\n \n\n#### Something You Have \n\nExample: \n\n```text\n     Smartphone \n     Security Key \n```\n\n#### Something You Are \n\nExample: \n\n```texy\n     Fingerprint \n\n     Face Recognition \n```\n \n\n### Example \n\nOnline banking commonly requires: \n\n```text\n     Password \n     + \n     Verification Code \n```\n\nEven if a password is stolen, the account remains better protected. ","resultHTML":"<section data-type=\"sect1\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture09-c3502-multifactor-authentication-mfa\">\n<h1>Multi-Factor Authentication (MFA)</h1>\n<p>Passwords alone are often insufficient.</p>\n<p>Multi-Factor Authentication adds additional verification steps.</p>\n<section data-type=\"sect2\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture09-c3502-authentication-factors\">\n<h1>Authentication Factors</h1>\n<section data-type=\"sect3\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture09-c3502-something-you-know\">\n<h1>Something You Know</h1>\n<p>Example:</p>\n<pre data-type=\"program-listing\" data-code-language=\"text\">     Password </pre>\n</section>\n<section data-type=\"sect3\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture09-c3502-something-you-have\">\n<h1>Something You Have</h1>\n<p>Example:</p>\n<pre data-type=\"program-listing\" data-code-language=\"text\">     Smartphone \n     Security Key </pre>\n</section>\n<section data-type=\"sect3\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture09-c3502-something-you-are\">\n<h1>Something You Are</h1>\n<p>Example:</p>\n<pre data-type=\"program-listing\" data-code-language=\"texy\">     Fingerprint \n\n     Face Recognition </pre>\n</section>\n</section>\n<section data-type=\"sect2\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture09-c3502-example\">\n<h1>Example</h1>\n<p>Online banking commonly requires:</p>\n<pre data-type=\"program-listing\" data-code-language=\"text\">     Password \n     + \n     Verification Code </pre>\n<p>Even if a password is stolen, the account remains better protected.</p>\n</section>\n</section>\n","hidden":true,"type":"markdown","translations":{"Dutch":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"2eb159069d8eb059f2871bac756309265c048110888ad6d10e1ea68ff80d6ae3","markdown":"## Multi-Factor Authentication (MFA)\n\nWachtwoorden alleen zijn vaak onvoldoende.\n\nMulti-Factor Authentication voegt extra verificatiestappen toe.\n\n\n\n### Authenticatiefactoren\n\n#### Iets wat je weet\n\nVoorbeeld:\n\n```text\n     Password \n```\n\n\n#### Iets wat je hebt\n\nVoorbeeld:\n\n```text\n     Smartphone \n     Security Key \n```\n\n#### Iets wat je bent\n\nVoorbeeld:\n\n```texy\n     Fingerprint \n\n     Face Recognition \n```\n\n\n### Voorbeeld\n\nOnline bankieren vereist doorgaans:\n\n```text\n     Password \n     + \n     Verification Code \n```\n\nZelfs als een wachtwoord wordt gestolen, blijft het account beter beschermd."},"French":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"2eb159069d8eb059f2871bac756309265c048110888ad6d10e1ea68ff80d6ae3","markdown":"## Authentification multifacteur (MFA) \n\nLes mots de passe seuls sont souvent insuffisants. \n\nL'authentification multifacteur ajoute des étapes de vérification supplémentaires. \n\n \n\n### Facteurs d'authentification \n\n#### Quelque chose que vous savez \n\nExemple : \n\n```text\n     Password \n```\n \n\n#### Quelque chose que vous possédez \n\nExemple : \n\n```text\n     Smartphone \n     Security Key \n```\n\n#### Quelque chose que vous êtes \n\nExemple : \n\n```texy\n     Fingerprint \n\n     Face Recognition \n```\n \n\n### Exemple \n\nLes services bancaires en ligne exigent généralement : \n\n```text\n     Password \n     + \n     Verification Code \n```\n\nMême si un mot de passe est volé, le compte reste mieux protégé. "}},"translationSource":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"2eb159069d8eb059f2871bac756309265c048110888ad6d10e1ea68ff80d6ae3","language":"English"}},{"input":"## Introduction to Cryptography \n\nCryptography is the science of protecting information using mathematical techniques. \n\n \n\n### Goals \n\nCryptography helps provide: \n\n- Confidentiality \n\n- Integrity \n\n- Authentication \n\n \n\n### Everyday Examples \n\nCryptography protects: \n\n- Online banking \n\n- Messaging applications \n\n- E-commerce \n\n- Digital signatures \n\nMost Internet users rely on cryptography daily. ","output":"","result":"## Introduction to Cryptography \n\nCryptography is the science of protecting information using mathematical techniques. \n\n \n\n### Goals \n\nCryptography helps provide: \n\n- Confidentiality \n\n- Integrity \n\n- Authentication \n\n \n\n### Everyday Examples \n\nCryptography protects: \n\n- Online banking \n\n- Messaging applications \n\n- E-commerce \n\n- Digital signatures \n\nMost Internet users rely on cryptography daily. ","resultHTML":"<section data-type=\"sect1\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture09-c3503-introduction-to-cryptography\">\n<h1>Introduction to Cryptography</h1>\n<p>Cryptography is the science of protecting information using mathematical techniques.</p>\n<section data-type=\"sect2\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture09-c3503-goals\">\n<h1>Goals</h1>\n<p>Cryptography helps provide:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Confidentiality</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Integrity</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Authentication</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</section>\n<section data-type=\"sect2\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture09-c3503-everyday-examples\">\n<h1>Everyday Examples</h1>\n<p>Cryptography protects:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Online banking</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Messaging applications</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>E-commerce</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Digital signatures</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Most Internet users rely on cryptography daily.</p>\n</section>\n</section>\n","hidden":true,"type":"markdown","translations":{"Dutch":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"cd070b094296a5e026d59afce8cdeb7ea60751196f053b9eabbb59d82e4c9a93","markdown":"## Inleiding tot Cryptografie \n\nCryptografie is de wetenschap die informatie beschermt met behulp van wiskundige technieken. \n\n \n\n### Doelstellingen \n\nCryptografie helpt bij het bieden van: \n\n- Vertrouwelijkheid \n\n- Integriteit \n\n- Authenticatie \n\n \n\n### Alledaagse voorbeelden \n\nCryptografie beschermt: \n\n- Online bankieren \n\n- Berichtentoepassingen \n\n- E-commerce \n\n- Digitale handtekeningen \n\nDe meeste internetgebruikers vertrouwen dagelijks op cryptografie. "},"French":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"cd070b094296a5e026d59afce8cdeb7ea60751196f053b9eabbb59d82e4c9a93","markdown":"## Introduction à la cryptographie \n\nLa cryptographie est la science qui protège l'information à l'aide de techniques mathématiques. \n\n \n\n### Objectifs \n\nLa cryptographie permet d'assurer : \n\n- La confidentialité \n\n- L'intégrité \n\n- L'authentification \n\n \n\n### Exemples du quotidien \n\nLa cryptographie protège : \n\n- Les opérations bancaires en ligne \n\n- Les applications de messagerie \n\n- Le commerce électronique \n\n- Les signatures numériques \n\nLa plupart des utilisateurs d'Internet font appel à la cryptographie au quotidien. \n"}},"translationSource":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"cd070b094296a5e026d59afce8cdeb7ea60751196f053b9eabbb59d82e4c9a93","language":"English"}},{"input":"## Encryption \n\nEncryption converts readable information into an unreadable form. \n\n \n\n### Plaintext \n\nOriginal information. \n\nExample: \n\n```text\n     Exam starts at 09:00 \n```\n \n\n### Ciphertext \n\nEncrypted information. \n\nExample: \n\n```text\n     XJ4P9MQL7... \n```\n \n\n### Principle \n\n```text\n     Plaintext \n     ↓ \n     Encryption \n     ↓ \n     Ciphertext \n```\n\nOnly authorized parties can recover the original information. ","output":"","result":"## Encryption \n\nEncryption converts readable information into an unreadable form. \n\n \n\n### Plaintext \n\nOriginal information. \n\nExample: \n\n```text\n     Exam starts at 09:00 \n```\n \n\n### Ciphertext \n\nEncrypted information. \n\nExample: \n\n```text\n     XJ4P9MQL7... \n```\n \n\n### Principle \n\n```text\n     Plaintext \n     ↓ \n     Encryption \n     ↓ \n     Ciphertext \n```\n\nOnly authorized parties can recover the original information. ","resultHTML":"<section data-type=\"sect1\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture09-c3504-encryption\">\n<h1>Encryption</h1>\n<p>Encryption converts readable information into an unreadable form.</p>\n<section data-type=\"sect2\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture09-c3504-plaintext\">\n<h1>Plaintext</h1>\n<p>Original information.</p>\n<p>Example:</p>\n<pre data-type=\"program-listing\" data-code-language=\"text\">     Exam starts at 09:00 </pre>\n</section>\n<section data-type=\"sect2\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture09-c3504-ciphertext\">\n<h1>Ciphertext</h1>\n<p>Encrypted information.</p>\n<p>Example:</p>\n<pre data-type=\"program-listing\" data-code-language=\"text\">     XJ4P9MQL7... </pre>\n</section>\n<section data-type=\"sect2\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture09-c3504-principle\">\n<h1>Principle</h1>\n<pre data-type=\"program-listing\" data-code-language=\"text\">     Plaintext \n     ↓ \n     Encryption \n     ↓ \n     Ciphertext </pre>\n<p>Only authorized parties can recover the original information.</p>\n</section>\n</section>\n","hidden":true,"type":"markdown","translations":{"Dutch":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"cf9845cd94c98c032ad8e4e6be1529cbb53deb9d8f9f2cc72550c8046fffd7b0","markdown":"## Encryptie \n\nEncryptie zet leesbare informatie om in een onleesbare vorm. \n\n \n\n### Platte tekst \n\nOorspronkelijke informatie. \n\nVoorbeeld: \n\n```text\n     Exam starts at 09:00 \n```\n \n\n### Cijfertekst \n\nVersleutelde informatie. \n\nVoorbeeld: \n\n```text\n     XJ4P9MQL7... \n```\n \n\n### Principe \n\n```text\n     Plaintext \n     ↓ \n     Encryption \n     ↓ \n     Ciphertext \n```\n\nAlleen bevoegde partijen kunnen de oorspronkelijke informatie terughalen. "},"French":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"cf9845cd94c98c032ad8e4e6be1529cbb53deb9d8f9f2cc72550c8046fffd7b0","markdown":"## Chiffrement \n\nLe chiffrement convertit une information lisible en une forme illisible. \n\n \n\n### Texte en clair \n\nInformation originale. \n\nExemple : \n\n```text\n     Exam starts at 09:00 \n```\n \n\n### Texte chiffré \n\nInformation chiffrée. \n\nExemple : \n\n```text\n     XJ4P9MQL7... \n```\n \n\n### Principe \n\n```text\n     Plaintext \n     ↓ \n     Encryption \n     ↓ \n     Ciphertext \n```\n\nSeules les parties autorisées peuvent récupérer l'information originale. "}},"translationSource":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"cf9845cd94c98c032ad8e4e6be1529cbb53deb9d8f9f2cc72550c8046fffd7b0","language":"English"}},{"input":"## Keys \n\nEncryption depends on a key. \n\nA key is secret information controlling encryption and decryption. \n\n \n\n### Analogy \n\nThink of a key for a physical lock. \n\nWithout the key: \n\n```text\n     Access denied \n```\n\nCryptographic keys function similarly. ","output":"","result":"## Keys \n\nEncryption depends on a key. \n\nA key is secret information controlling encryption and decryption. \n\n \n\n### Analogy \n\nThink of a key for a physical lock. \n\nWithout the key: \n\n```text\n     Access denied \n```\n\nCryptographic keys function similarly. ","resultHTML":"<section data-type=\"sect1\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture09-c3505-keys\">\n<h1>Keys</h1>\n<p>Encryption depends on a key.</p>\n<p>A key is secret information controlling encryption and decryption.</p>\n<section data-type=\"sect2\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture09-c3505-analogy\">\n<h1>Analogy</h1>\n<p>Think of a key for a physical lock.</p>\n<p>Without the key:</p>\n<pre data-type=\"program-listing\" data-code-language=\"text\">     Access denied </pre>\n<p>Cryptographic keys function similarly.</p>\n</section>\n</section>\n","hidden":true,"type":"markdown","translations":{"Dutch":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"aa66eb5bf532996c63f464019e2f1363750ae86fe985250f3304b289267ff1bc","markdown":"## Sleutels \n\nVersleuteling is afhankelijk van een sleutel. \n\nEen sleutel is geheime informatie die versleuteling en ontsleuteling bepaalt. \n\n \n\n### Analogie \n\nDenk aan een sleutel voor een fysiek slot. \n\nZonder de sleutel: \n\n```text\n     Access denied \n```\n\nCryptografische sleutels werken op vergelijkbare wijze. "},"French":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"aa66eb5bf532996c63f464019e2f1363750ae86fe985250f3304b289267ff1bc","markdown":"## Clés \n\nLe chiffrement dépend d'une clé. \n\nUne clé est une information secrète qui contrôle le chiffrement et le déchiffrement. \n\n \n\n### Analogie \n\nPensez à une clé pour une serrure physique. \n\nSans la clé : \n\n```text\n     Access denied \n```\n\nLes clés cryptographiques fonctionnent de manière similaire. "}},"translationSource":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"aa66eb5bf532996c63f464019e2f1363750ae86fe985250f3304b289267ff1bc","language":"English"}},{"input":"## Symmetric Encryption \n\nSymmetric encryption uses one shared key. \n\n \n\n### Process \n\n```text\n     Sender \n     ↓ \n     Shared Key \n     ↓ \n     Receiver \n```\n\nBoth parties know the same secret. \n\n \n\n### Advantages \n\n- Fast \n\n- Efficient \n\n \n\n### Challenge \n\nThe key must be shared securely beforehand. ","output":"","result":"## Symmetric Encryption \n\nSymmetric encryption uses one shared key. \n\n \n\n### Process \n\n```text\n     Sender \n     ↓ \n     Shared Key \n     ↓ \n     Receiver \n```\n\nBoth parties know the same secret. \n\n \n\n### Advantages \n\n- Fast \n\n- Efficient \n\n \n\n### Challenge \n\nThe key must be shared securely beforehand. ","resultHTML":"<section data-type=\"sect1\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture09-c3506-symmetric-encryption\">\n<h1>Symmetric Encryption</h1>\n<p>Symmetric encryption uses one shared key.</p>\n<section data-type=\"sect2\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture09-c3506-process\">\n<h1>Process</h1>\n<pre data-type=\"program-listing\" data-code-language=\"text\">     Sender \n     ↓ \n     Shared Key \n     ↓ \n     Receiver </pre>\n<p>Both parties know the same secret.</p>\n</section>\n<section data-type=\"sect2\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture09-c3506-advantages\">\n<h1>Advantages</h1>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Fast</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Efficient</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</section>\n<section data-type=\"sect2\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture09-c3506-challenge\">\n<h1>Challenge</h1>\n<p>The key must be shared securely beforehand.</p>\n</section>\n</section>\n","hidden":true,"type":"markdown","translations":{"Dutch":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"ca061b41078eba1ec96adbe57c438ddbc9d4a16dbc9f5ca5278c38c7664c01ba","markdown":"## Symmetrische Versleuteling \n\nSymmetrische versleuteling gebruikt één gedeelde sleutel. \n\n \n\n### Proces \n\n```text\n     Sender \n     ↓ \n     Shared Key \n     ↓ \n     Receiver \n```\n\nBeide partijen kennen hetzelfde geheim. \n\n \n\n### Voordelen \n\n- Snel \n\n- Efficiënt \n\n \n\n### Uitdaging \n\nDe sleutel moet vooraf veilig worden gedeeld. "},"French":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"ca061b41078eba1ec96adbe57c438ddbc9d4a16dbc9f5ca5278c38c7664c01ba","markdown":"## Chiffrement symétrique \n\nLe chiffrement symétrique utilise une seule clé partagée. \n\n \n\n### Processus \n\n```text\n     Sender \n     ↓ \n     Shared Key \n     ↓ \n     Receiver \n```\n\nLes deux parties connaissent le même secret. \n\n \n\n### Avantages \n\n- Rapide \n\n- Efficace \n\n \n\n### Défi \n\nLa clé doit être partagée de manière sécurisée au préalable. "}},"translationSource":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"ca061b41078eba1ec96adbe57c438ddbc9d4a16dbc9f5ca5278c38c7664c01ba","language":"English"}},{"input":"## Asymmetric Encryption \n\nAsymmetric encryption uses two keys. \n\n \n\n### Public Key \n\nCan be shared openly. \n\n \n\n### Private Key \n\nMust remain secret. \n\n \n\n### Example \n\nAnyone can lock a box using the public key. \n\nOnly the owner can open it using the private key. \n\n \n\n### Why It Matters \n\nAsymmetric cryptography enables secure communication between people who have never met. \n\nIt is fundamental to Internet security. ","output":"","result":"## Asymmetric Encryption \n\nAsymmetric encryption uses two keys. \n\n \n\n### Public Key \n\nCan be shared openly. \n\n \n\n### Private Key \n\nMust remain secret. \n\n \n\n### Example \n\nAnyone can lock a box using the public key. \n\nOnly the owner can open it using the private key. \n\n \n\n### Why It Matters \n\nAsymmetric cryptography enables secure communication between people who have never met. \n\nIt is fundamental to Internet security. ","resultHTML":"<section data-type=\"sect1\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture09-c3507-asymmetric-encryption\">\n<h1>Asymmetric Encryption</h1>\n<p>Asymmetric encryption uses two keys.</p>\n<section data-type=\"sect2\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture09-c3507-public-key\">\n<h1>Public Key</h1>\n<p>Can be shared openly.</p>\n</section>\n<section data-type=\"sect2\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture09-c3507-private-key\">\n<h1>Private Key</h1>\n<p>Must remain secret.</p>\n</section>\n<section data-type=\"sect2\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture09-c3507-example\">\n<h1>Example</h1>\n<p>Anyone can lock a box using the public key.</p>\n<p>Only the owner can open it using the private key.</p>\n</section>\n<section data-type=\"sect2\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture09-c3507-why-it-matters\">\n<h1>Why It Matters</h1>\n<p>Asymmetric cryptography enables secure communication between people who have never met.</p>\n<p>It is fundamental to Internet security.</p>\n</section>\n</section>\n","hidden":true,"type":"markdown","translations":{"Dutch":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"a27c44f05f07cb41c594276d183e4e833938b528c50aa8aaa4e335dc4dfba60f","markdown":"## Asymmetrische versleuteling \n\nAsymmetrische versleuteling gebruikt twee sleutels. \n\n \n\n### Publieke sleutel \n\nKan openlijk gedeeld worden. \n\n \n\n### Privésleutel \n\nMoet geheim blijven. \n\n \n\n### Voorbeeld \n\nledereen kan een doos vergrendelen met de publieke sleutel. \n\nAlleen de eigenaar kan hem openen met de privésleutel. \n\n \n\n### Waarom het belangrijk is \n\nAsymmetrische cryptografie maakt veilige communicatie mogelijk tussen mensen die elkaar nooit hebben ontmoet. \n\nHet is fundamenteel voor de veiligheid van het internet. "},"French":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"a27c44f05f07cb41c594276d183e4e833938b528c50aa8aaa4e335dc4dfba60f","markdown":"## Chiffrement asymétrique \n\nLe chiffrement asymétrique utilise deux clés. \n\n \n\n### Clé publique \n\nPeut être partagée ouvertement. \n\n \n\n### Clé privée \n\nDoit rester secrète. \n\n \n\n### Exemple \n\nN'importe qui peut verrouiller une boîte en utilisant la clé publique. \n\nSeul le propriétaire peut l'ouvrir en utilisant la clé privée. \n\n \n\n### Pourquoi c'est important \n\nLa cryptographie asymétrique permet une communication sécurisée entre des personnes qui ne se sont jamais rencontrées. \n\nElle est fondamentale pour la sécurité d'Internet. "}},"translationSource":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"a27c44f05f07cb41c594276d183e4e833938b528c50aa8aaa4e335dc4dfba60f","language":"English"}},{"input":"## Hash Functions \n\nA hash function transforms data into a fixed-size value. \n\n \n\n### Example \n\nDocument: \n\n```text\n     Hello \n```\n\nHash: \n\n```text\n     A94A8FE5... \n```\n \n\n### Properties \n\nSmall changes in input produce large changes in output. \n\n \n\n#### Example \n\n```text\n     Hello \n```\n\nand \n```text\n     hello \n```\n\nproduce very different hashes. \n\n \n\n### Uses \n\nHashing is used for: \n\n- Password storage \n\n- Data integrity \n\n- Digital signatures ","output":"","result":"## Hash Functions \n\nA hash function transforms data into a fixed-size value. \n\n \n\n### Example \n\nDocument: \n\n```text\n     Hello \n```\n\nHash: \n\n```text\n     A94A8FE5... \n```\n \n\n### Properties \n\nSmall changes in input produce large changes in output. \n\n \n\n#### Example \n\n```text\n     Hello \n```\n\nand \n```text\n     hello \n```\n\nproduce very different hashes. \n\n \n\n### Uses \n\nHashing is used for: \n\n- Password storage \n\n- Data integrity \n\n- Digital signatures ","resultHTML":"<section data-type=\"sect1\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture09-c3508-hash-functions\">\n<h1>Hash Functions</h1>\n<p>A hash function transforms data into a fixed-size value.</p>\n<section data-type=\"sect2\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture09-c3508-example\">\n<h1>Example</h1>\n<p>Document:</p>\n<pre data-type=\"program-listing\" data-code-language=\"text\">     Hello </pre>\n<p>Hash:</p>\n<pre data-type=\"program-listing\" data-code-language=\"text\">     A94A8FE5... </pre>\n</section>\n<section data-type=\"sect2\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture09-c3508-properties\">\n<h1>Properties</h1>\n<p>Small changes in input produce large changes in output.</p>\n<section data-type=\"sect3\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture09-c3508-example-2\">\n<h1>Example</h1>\n<pre data-type=\"program-listing\" data-code-language=\"text\">     Hello </pre>\n<p>and</p>\n<pre data-type=\"program-listing\" data-code-language=\"text\">     hello </pre>\n<p>produce very different hashes.</p>\n</section>\n</section>\n<section data-type=\"sect2\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture09-c3508-uses\">\n<h1>Uses</h1>\n<p>Hashing is used for:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Password storage</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Data integrity</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Digital signatures</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</section>\n</section>\n","hidden":true,"type":"markdown","translations":{"Dutch":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"b90530586442eef5280778f94643fecfba3a8bd8783f012586ec288ba8d2ed63","markdown":"## Hashfuncties\n\nEen hashfunctie zet gegevens om in een waarde van vaste grootte.\n\n\n\n### Voorbeeld\n\nDocument:\n\n```text\n     Hello \n```\n\nHash:\n\n```text\n     A94A8FE5... \n```\n\n\n### Eigenschappen\n\nKleine veranderingen in de invoer veroorzaken grote veranderingen in de uitvoer.\n\n\n\n#### Voorbeeld\n\n```text\n     Hello \n```\n\nen\n```text\n     hello \n```\n\nleveren zeer verschillende hashes op.\n\n\n\n### Toepassingen\n\nHashing wordt gebruikt voor:\n\n- Opslag van wachtwoorden\n\n- Gegevensintegriteit\n\n- Digitale handtekeningen"},"French":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"b90530586442eef5280778f94643fecfba3a8bd8783f012586ec288ba8d2ed63","markdown":"## Fonctions de hachage \n\nUne fonction de hachage transforme des données en une valeur de taille fixe. \n\n \n\n### Exemple \n\nDocument : \n\n```text\n     Hello \n```\n\nHachage : \n\n```text\n     A94A8FE5... \n```\n \n\n### Propriétés \n\nDe petits changements dans l'entrée produisent de grands changements dans la sortie. \n\n \n\n#### Exemple \n\n```text\n     Hello \n```\n\net \n```text\n     hello \n```\n\nproduisent des hachages très différents. \n\n \n\n### Utilisations \n\nLe hachage est utilisé pour : \n\n- Le stockage des mots de passe \n\n- L'intégrité des données \n\n- Les signatures numériques "}},"translationSource":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"b90530586442eef5280778f94643fecfba3a8bd8783f012586ec288ba8d2ed63","language":"English"}},{"input":"## Digital Signatures \n\nDigital signatures help answer two questions: \n\n```text\n     Who created this document? \n     Has it been modified? \n```\n \n\n### Example \n\nSuppose a university issues a diploma electronically. \n\nA digital signature helps recipients verify: \n\n- The source is authentic. \n\n- The document has not been altered. \n\n \n\n### Benefits \n\nDigital signatures support: \n\n- Authenticity \n\n- Integrity \n\n- Non-repudiation ","output":"","result":"## Digital Signatures \n\nDigital signatures help answer two questions: \n\n```text\n     Who created this document? \n     Has it been modified? \n```\n \n\n### Example \n\nSuppose a university issues a diploma electronically. \n\nA digital signature helps recipients verify: \n\n- The source is authentic. \n\n- The document has not been altered. \n\n \n\n### Benefits \n\nDigital signatures support: \n\n- Authenticity \n\n- Integrity \n\n- Non-repudiation ","resultHTML":"<section data-type=\"sect1\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture09-c3509-digital-signatures\">\n<h1>Digital Signatures</h1>\n<p>Digital signatures help answer two questions:</p>\n<pre data-type=\"program-listing\" data-code-language=\"text\">     Who created this document? \n     Has it been modified? </pre>\n<section data-type=\"sect2\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture09-c3509-example\">\n<h1>Example</h1>\n<p>Suppose a university issues a diploma electronically.</p>\n<p>A digital signature helps recipients verify:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>The source is authentic.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>The document has not been altered.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</section>\n<section data-type=\"sect2\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture09-c3509-benefits\">\n<h1>Benefits</h1>\n<p>Digital signatures support:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Authenticity</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Integrity</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Non-repudiation</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</section>\n</section>\n","hidden":true,"type":"markdown","translations":{"Dutch":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"05939fd59009aec9cc142ae452f9c65605af8493b63050703895a18475065ca8","markdown":"## Digitale Handtekeningen \n\nDigitale handtekeningen helpen twee vragen te beantwoorden: \n\n```text\n     Who created this document? \n     Has it been modified? \n```\n \n\n### Voorbeeld \n\nStel dat een universiteit elektronisch een diploma uitreikt. \n\nEen digitale handtekening helpt ontvangers om te controleren: \n\n- De bron is authentiek. \n\n- Het document is niet gewijzigd. \n\n \n\n### Voordelen \n\nDigitale handtekeningen ondersteunen: \n\n- Authenticiteit \n\n- Integriteit \n\n- Onweerlegbaarheid "},"French":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"05939fd59009aec9cc142ae452f9c65605af8493b63050703895a18475065ca8","markdown":"## Signatures numériques \n\nLes signatures numériques aident à répondre à deux questions : \n\n```text\n     Who created this document? \n     Has it been modified? \n```\n \n\n### Exemple \n\nSupposons qu'une université délivre un diplôme électroniquement. \n\nUne signature numérique aide les destinataires à vérifier : \n\n- La source est authentique. \n\n- Le document n'a pas été altéré. \n\n \n\n### Avantages \n\nLes signatures numériques permettent de garantir : \n\n- L'authenticité \n\n- L'intégrité \n\n- La non-répudiation "}},"translationSource":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"05939fd59009aec9cc142ae452f9c65605af8493b63050703895a18475065ca8","language":"English"}},{"input":"## Malware \n\nMalware stands for: \n\n```text\n     Malicious Software \n```\n\nSoftware deliberately designed to cause harm. \n\n \n\n### Examples of Malware \n\n#### Virus \n\nAttaches itself to other files. \n\n \n\n#### Worm \n\nSpreads automatically through networks. \n\n \n\n#### Trojan Horse \n\nPretends to be legitimate software. \n\n \n\n#### Ransomware \n\nEncrypts data and demands payment. \n\n \n\n### Impact \n\nMalware can: \n\n- Destroy data \n\n- Steal information \n\n- Disrupt services ","output":"","result":"## Malware \n\nMalware stands for: \n\n```text\n     Malicious Software \n```\n\nSoftware deliberately designed to cause harm. \n\n \n\n### Examples of Malware \n\n#### Virus \n\nAttaches itself to other files. \n\n \n\n#### Worm \n\nSpreads automatically through networks. \n\n \n\n#### Trojan Horse \n\nPretends to be legitimate software. \n\n \n\n#### Ransomware \n\nEncrypts data and demands payment. \n\n \n\n### Impact \n\nMalware can: \n\n- Destroy data \n\n- Steal information \n\n- Disrupt services ","resultHTML":"<section data-type=\"sect1\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture09-c3510-malware\">\n<h1>Malware</h1>\n<p>Malware stands for:</p>\n<pre data-type=\"program-listing\" data-code-language=\"text\">     Malicious Software </pre>\n<p>Software deliberately designed to cause harm.</p>\n<section data-type=\"sect2\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture09-c3510-examples-of-malware\">\n<h1>Examples of Malware</h1>\n<section data-type=\"sect3\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture09-c3510-virus\">\n<h1>Virus</h1>\n<p>Attaches itself to other files.</p>\n</section>\n<section data-type=\"sect3\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture09-c3510-worm\">\n<h1>Worm</h1>\n<p>Spreads automatically through networks.</p>\n</section>\n<section data-type=\"sect3\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture09-c3510-trojan-horse\">\n<h1>Trojan Horse</h1>\n<p>Pretends to be legitimate software.</p>\n</section>\n<section data-type=\"sect3\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture09-c3510-ransomware\">\n<h1>Ransomware</h1>\n<p>Encrypts data and demands payment.</p>\n</section>\n</section>\n<section data-type=\"sect2\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture09-c3510-impact\">\n<h1>Impact</h1>\n<p>Malware can:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Destroy data</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Steal information</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Disrupt services</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</section>\n</section>\n","hidden":true,"type":"markdown","translations":{"Dutch":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"0e6b35abd941b307e8ca6a4c84136bff6950e8980e3885e54b35fa0efa6e1a8a","markdown":"## Malware\n\nMalware staat voor:\n\n```text\n     Malicious Software \n```\n\nSoftware die opzettelijk is ontworpen om schade te veroorzaken.\n\n \n\n### Voorbeelden van Malware\n\n#### Virus\n\nHecht zich aan andere bestanden.\n\n \n\n#### Worm\n\nVerspreidt zich automatisch via netwerken.\n\n \n\n#### Trojaans Paard\n\nDoet zich voor als legitieme software.\n\n \n\n#### Ransomware\n\nVersleutelt gegevens en eist losgeld.\n\n \n\n### Impact\n\nMalware kan:\n\n- Gegevens vernietigen\n\n- Informatie stelen\n\n- Diensten verstoren"},"French":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"0e6b35abd941b307e8ca6a4c84136bff6950e8980e3885e54b35fa0efa6e1a8a","markdown":"## Malware \n\nMalware signifie : \n\n```text\n     Malicious Software \n```\n\nLogiciel délibérément conçu pour causer des dommages. \n\n \n\n### Exemples de Malware \n\n#### Virus \n\nS'attache à d'autres fichiers. \n\n \n\n#### Ver \n\nSe propage automatiquement à travers les réseaux. \n\n \n\n#### Cheval de Troie \n\nPrétend être un logiciel légitime. \n\n \n\n#### Rançongiciel \n\nChiffre les données et exige un paiement. \n\n \n\n### Impact \n\nLes logiciels malveillants peuvent : \n\n- Détruire des données \n\n- Voler des informations \n\n- Perturber des services "}},"translationSource":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"0e6b35abd941b307e8ca6a4c84136bff6950e8980e3885e54b35fa0efa6e1a8a","language":"English"}},{"input":"## Social Engineering \n\nNot all attacks target computers directly. \n\nMany attacks target people. \n\nThis is called social engineering. \n\n \n\n### Definition \n\nSocial engineering manipulates individuals into revealing information or performing unsafe actions. \n\n \n\n### Why It Works \n\nHumans are often the weakest link in security. \n\nAttackers exploit: \n\n- Trust \n\n- Curiosity \n\n- Fear \n\n- Urgency ","output":"","result":"## Social Engineering \n\nNot all attacks target computers directly. \n\nMany attacks target people. \n\nThis is called social engineering. \n\n \n\n### Definition \n\nSocial engineering manipulates individuals into revealing information or performing unsafe actions. \n\n \n\n### Why It Works \n\nHumans are often the weakest link in security. \n\nAttackers exploit: \n\n- Trust \n\n- Curiosity \n\n- Fear \n\n- Urgency ","resultHTML":"<section data-type=\"sect1\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture09-c3511-social-engineering\">\n<h1>Social Engineering</h1>\n<p>Not all attacks target computers directly.</p>\n<p>Many attacks target people.</p>\n<p>This is called social engineering.</p>\n<section data-type=\"sect2\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture09-c3511-definition\">\n<h1>Definition</h1>\n<p>Social engineering manipulates individuals into revealing information or performing unsafe actions.</p>\n</section>\n<section data-type=\"sect2\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture09-c3511-why-it-works\">\n<h1>Why It Works</h1>\n<p>Humans are often the weakest link in security.</p>\n<p>Attackers exploit:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Trust</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Curiosity</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Fear</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Urgency</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</section>\n</section>\n","hidden":true,"type":"markdown","translations":{"Dutch":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"dc61dd661094fec43434187a9edf9ff4f24c3e79fa96c69e35fd09e48a357f24","markdown":"## Social Engineering \n\nNiet alle aanvallen richten zich rechtstreeks op computers. \n\nVeel aanvallen richten zich op mensen. \n\nDit wordt social engineering genoemd. \n\n \n\n### Definitie \n\nSocial engineering manipuleert individuen om informatie prijs te geven of onveilige handelingen uit te voeren. \n\n \n\n### Waarom Het Werkt \n\nMensen zijn vaak de zwakste schakel in beveiliging. \n\nAanvallers maken misbruik van: \n\n- Vertrouwen \n\n- Nieuwsgierigheid \n\n- Angst \n\n- Urgentie "},"French":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"dc61dd661094fec43434187a9edf9ff4f24c3e79fa96c69e35fd09e48a357f24","markdown":"## Ingénierie sociale \n\nToutes les attaques ne ciblent pas directement les ordinateurs. \n\nDe nombreuses attaques ciblent les personnes. \n\nC'est ce qu'on appelle l'ingénierie sociale. \n\n \n\n### Définition \n\nL'ingénierie sociale manipule des individus pour qu'ils révèlent des informations ou effectuent des actions dangereuses. \n\n \n\n### Pourquoi ça fonctionne \n\nLes humains sont souvent le maillon le plus faible de la sécurité. \n\nLes attaquants exploitent : \n\n- La confiance \n\n- La curiosité \n\n- La peur \n\n- L'urgence "}},"translationSource":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"dc61dd661094fec43434187a9edf9ff4f24c3e79fa96c69e35fd09e48a357f24","language":"English"}},{"input":"## Phishing \n\nPhishing is one of the most common cyberattacks. \n\n \n\n### Example \n\nAn email claims:\n\n```text\n     Your account will be closed. \n     Click here immediately. \n```\n\nThe message appears legitimate. \n\nHowever, it leads to a fraudulent website. \n\n \n\n### Goal \n\nThe attacker attempts to steal: \n\n- Passwords \n\n- Credit card data \n\n- Personal information \n\n \n\n### Warning Signs \n\n- Spelling errors (no the case when AI is used)\n\n- Unexpected urgency \n\n- Suspicious links \n\n- Requests for confidential information ","output":"","result":"## Phishing \n\nPhishing is one of the most common cyberattacks. \n\n \n\n### Example \n\nAn email claims:\n\n```text\n     Your account will be closed. \n     Click here immediately. \n```\n\nThe message appears legitimate. \n\nHowever, it leads to a fraudulent website. \n\n \n\n### Goal \n\nThe attacker attempts to steal: \n\n- Passwords \n\n- Credit card data \n\n- Personal information \n\n \n\n### Warning Signs \n\n- Spelling errors (no the case when AI is used)\n\n- Unexpected urgency \n\n- Suspicious links \n\n- Requests for confidential information ","resultHTML":"<section data-type=\"sect1\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture09-c3512-phishing\">\n<h1>Phishing</h1>\n<p>Phishing is one of the most common cyberattacks.</p>\n<section data-type=\"sect2\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture09-c3512-example\">\n<h1>Example</h1>\n<p>An email claims:</p>\n<pre data-type=\"program-listing\" data-code-language=\"text\">     Your account will be closed. \n     Click here immediately. </pre>\n<p>The message appears legitimate.</p>\n<p>However, it leads to a fraudulent website.</p>\n</section>\n<section data-type=\"sect2\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture09-c3512-goal\">\n<h1>Goal</h1>\n<p>The attacker attempts to steal:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Passwords</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Credit card data</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Personal information</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</section>\n<section data-type=\"sect2\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture09-c3512-warning-signs\">\n<h1>Warning Signs</h1>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Spelling errors (no the case when AI is used)</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Unexpected urgency</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Suspicious links</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Requests for confidential information</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</section>\n</section>\n","hidden":true,"type":"markdown","translations":{"Dutch":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"ff1f3caeeafc168ffcd57549b0c58d1dfeff5bbada3a7efc7d5de492edf820a7","markdown":"## Phishing \n\nPhishing is een van de meest voorkomende cyberaanvallen. \n\n \n\n### Voorbeeld \n\nEen e-mail beweert:\n\n```text\n     Your account will be closed. \n     Click here immediately. \n```\n\nHet bericht lijkt legitiem. \n\nToch leidt het naar een frauduleuze website. \n\n \n\n### Doel \n\nDe aanvaller probeert te stelen: \n\n- Wachtwoorden \n\n- Creditcardgegevens \n\n- Persoonlijke informatie \n\n \n\n### Waarschuwingssignalen \n\n- Spelfouten (niet het geval wanneer AI wordt gebruikt)\n\n- Onverwachte urgentie \n\n- Verdachte links \n\n- Verzoeken om vertrouwelijke informatie "},"French":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"ff1f3caeeafc168ffcd57549b0c58d1dfeff5bbada3a7efc7d5de492edf820a7","markdown":"## Hameçonnage \n\nL'hameçonnage est l'une des cyberattaques les plus courantes. \n\n \n\n### Exemple \n\nUn e-mail prétend :\n\n```text\n     Your account will be closed. \n     Click here immediately. \n```\n\nLe message semble légitime. \n\nCependant, il mène vers un site web frauduleux. \n\n \n\n### Objectif \n\nL'attaquant tente de voler : \n\n- Les mots de passe \n\n- Les données de carte de crédit \n\n- Les informations personnelles \n\n \n\n### Signes d'alerte \n\n- Fautes d'orthographe (ce n'est pas le cas lorsque l'IA est utilisée)\n\n- Urgence inattendue \n\n- Liens suspects \n\n- Demandes d'informations confidentielles "}},"translationSource":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"ff1f3caeeafc168ffcd57549b0c58d1dfeff5bbada3a7efc7d5de492edf820a7","language":"English"}},{"input":"## Security Best Practices \n\nCybersecurity is not only about technology. \n\nUser behavior matters greatly. \n\n \n\n### Keep Software Updated \n\nUpdates often fix security vulnerabilities. \n\n \n\n### Use Strong Passwords \n\nLong and unique passwords reduce risk. \n\n \n\n### Enable MFA \n\nAdds an extra layer of protection. \n\n \n\n### Be Skeptical \n\nQuestion unexpected messages and requests. \n\n \n\n### Backup Important Data \n\nBackups reduce the impact of: \n\n- Hardware failures \n\n- Ransomware \n\n- Accidental deletion \n\n \n\n### Protect Personal Information \n\nShare only information that is necessary. ","output":"","result":"## Security Best Practices \n\nCybersecurity is not only about technology. \n\nUser behavior matters greatly. \n\n \n\n### Keep Software Updated \n\nUpdates often fix security vulnerabilities. \n\n \n\n### Use Strong Passwords \n\nLong and unique passwords reduce risk. \n\n \n\n### Enable MFA \n\nAdds an extra layer of protection. \n\n \n\n### Be Skeptical \n\nQuestion unexpected messages and requests. \n\n \n\n### Backup Important Data \n\nBackups reduce the impact of: \n\n- Hardware failures \n\n- Ransomware \n\n- Accidental deletion \n\n \n\n### Protect Personal Information \n\nShare only information that is necessary. ","resultHTML":"<section data-type=\"sect1\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture09-c3513-security-best-practices\">\n<h1>Security Best Practices</h1>\n<p>Cybersecurity is not only about technology.</p>\n<p>User behavior matters greatly.</p>\n<section data-type=\"sect2\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture09-c3513-keep-software-updated\">\n<h1>Keep Software Updated</h1>\n<p>Updates often fix security vulnerabilities.</p>\n</section>\n<section data-type=\"sect2\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture09-c3513-use-strong-passwords\">\n<h1>Use Strong Passwords</h1>\n<p>Long and unique passwords reduce risk.</p>\n</section>\n<section data-type=\"sect2\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture09-c3513-enable-mfa\">\n<h1>Enable MFA</h1>\n<p>Adds an extra layer of protection.</p>\n</section>\n<section data-type=\"sect2\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture09-c3513-be-skeptical\">\n<h1>Be Skeptical</h1>\n<p>Question unexpected messages and requests.</p>\n</section>\n<section data-type=\"sect2\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture09-c3513-backup-important-data\">\n<h1>Backup Important Data</h1>\n<p>Backups reduce the impact of:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Hardware failures</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Ransomware</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Accidental deletion</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</section>\n<section data-type=\"sect2\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture09-c3513-protect-personal-information\">\n<h1>Protect Personal Information</h1>\n<p>Share only information that is necessary.</p>\n</section>\n</section>\n","hidden":true,"type":"markdown","translations":{"Dutch":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"313129c622a43faeacaa6358429b4ced7754e00281198e6c02cb0ef999bed132","markdown":"## Beveiligingsbest practices \n\nCyberbeveiliging gaat niet alleen over technologie. \n\nGebruikersgedrag is van groot belang. \n\n \n\n### Houd software up-to-date \nUpdates verhelpen vaak beveiligingslekken. \n\n \n\n### Gebruik sterke wachtwoorden \nLange en unieke wachtwoorden verminderen het risico. \n\n \n\n### Schakel MFA in \nVoegt een extra beveiligingslaag toe. \n\n \n\n### Wees achterdochtig \nStel onverwachte berichten en verzoeken in vraag. \n\n \n\n### Maak back-ups van belangrijke gegevens \nBack-ups beperken de impact van: \n\n- Hardwarestoringen \n\n- Ransomware \n\n- Onbedoelde verwijdering \n\n \n\n### Bescherm persoonlijke informatie \nDeel alleen informatie die noodzakelijk is. "},"French":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"313129c622a43faeacaa6358429b4ced7754e00281198e6c02cb0ef999bed132","markdown":"## Meilleures pratiques de sécurité \n\nLa cybersécurité ne concerne pas seulement la technologie. \n\nLe comportement de l'utilisateur compte énormément. \n\n \n\n### Maintenir les logiciels à jour \n\nLes mises à jour corrigent souvent des vulnérabilités de sécurité. \n\n \n\n### Utiliser des mots de passe forts \n\nDes mots de passe longs et uniques réduisent le risque. \n\n \n\n### Activer l'authentification multifacteur (MFA) \n\nAjoute une couche de protection supplémentaire. \n\n \n\n### Faire preuve de scepticisme \n\nRemettez en question les messages et demandes inattendus. \n\n \n\n### Sauvegarder les données importantes \n\nLes sauvegardes réduisent l'impact : \n\n- Des pannes matérielles \n\n- Des rançongiciels \n\n- Des suppressions accidentelles \n\n \n\n### Protéger les informations personnelles \n\nNe partagez que les informations nécessaires. "}},"translationSource":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"313129c622a43faeacaa6358429b4ced7754e00281198e6c02cb0ef999bed132","language":"English"}},{"input":"## Security in Everyday Life \n\nConsider a student's digital life. \n\n \n\n### Accounts \n\n- University account \n\n- Email account \n\n- Social media account \n\n \n\n### Devices \n\n- Smartphone \n\n- Laptop \n\n- Tablet \n\n \n\n### Data \n\n- Assignments \n\n- Personal photos \n\n- Financial information \n\nAll require protection. \n\nCybersecurity is therefore a practical life skill, not merely a technical subject.","output":"","result":"## Security in Everyday Life \n\nConsider a student's digital life. \n\n \n\n### Accounts \n\n- University account \n\n- Email account \n\n- Social media account \n\n \n\n### Devices \n\n- Smartphone \n\n- Laptop \n\n- Tablet \n\n \n\n### Data \n\n- Assignments \n\n- Personal photos \n\n- Financial information \n\nAll require protection. \n\nCybersecurity is therefore a practical life skill, not merely a technical subject.","resultHTML":"<section data-type=\"sect1\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture09-c3514-security-in-everyday-life\">\n<h1>Security in Everyday Life</h1>\n<p>Consider a student’s digital life.</p>\n<section data-type=\"sect2\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture09-c3514-accounts\">\n<h1>Accounts</h1>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>University account</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Email account</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Social media account</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</section>\n<section data-type=\"sect2\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture09-c3514-devices\">\n<h1>Devices</h1>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Smartphone</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Laptop</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Tablet</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</section>\n<section data-type=\"sect2\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture09-c3514-data\">\n<h1>Data</h1>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Assignments</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Personal photos</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Financial information</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>All require protection.</p>\n<p>Cybersecurity is therefore a practical life skill, not merely a technical subject.</p>\n</section>\n</section>\n","hidden":true,"type":"markdown","translations":{"Dutch":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"d4c707ba3ccc4aa03fb5b95289f4c6844935d968949970a01c4a997134ad6c74","markdown":"## Veiligheid in het Dagelijks Leven \n\nDenk aan het digitale leven van een student. \n\n \n\n### Accounts \n\n- Universiteitsaccount \n\n- E-mailaccount \n\n- Account op sociale media \n\n \n\n### Apparaten \n\n- Smartphone \n\n- Laptop \n\n- Tablet \n\n \n\n### Gegevens \n\n- Opdrachten \n\n- Persoonlijke foto's \n\n- Financiële informatie \n\nAl deze zaken vereisen bescherming. \n\nCyberveiligheid is daarom een praktische levensvaardigheid, niet louter een technisch vak."},"French":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"d4c707ba3ccc4aa03fb5b95289f4c6844935d968949970a01c4a997134ad6c74","markdown":"## La sécurité au quotidien \n\nPrenons l'exemple de la vie numérique d'un étudiant. \n\n \n\n### Comptes \n\n- Compte universitaire \n\n- Compte de messagerie \n\n- Compte de réseau social \n\n \n\n### Appareils \n\n- Smartphone \n\n- Ordinateur portable \n\n- Tablette \n\n \n\n### Données \n\n- Devoirs \n\n- Photos personnelles \n\n- Informations financières \n\nTous nécessitent une protection. \n\nLa cybersécurité est donc une compétence pratique de la vie courante, et pas seulement une matière technique."}},"translationSource":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"d4c707ba3ccc4aa03fb5b95289f4c6844935d968949970a01c4a997134ad6c74","language":"English"}},{"input":"## Summary \n\nIn this chapter we learned: \n\n- Cybersecurity protects systems, data, and services. \n\n- Assets, threats, vulnerabilities, and risks are fundamental security concepts. \n\n- Confidentiality, Integrity, and Availability form the CIA triad. \n\n- Authentication verifies identity. \n\n- Authorization determines permissions. \n\n- Strong passwords and MFA improve security. \n\n- Encryption protects confidential information. \n\n- Symmetric and asymmetric cryptography use different key models. \n\n- Hash functions support integrity verification. \n\n- Digital signatures provide authenticity and integrity. \n\n- Malware includes viruses, worms, trojans, and ransomware. \n\n- Social engineering attacks people rather than technology. \n\n- Phishing is one of the most common cyber threats. \n\n- Good security practices significantly reduce risk. ","output":"","result":"## Summary \n\nIn this chapter we learned: \n\n- Cybersecurity protects systems, data, and services. \n\n- Assets, threats, vulnerabilities, and risks are fundamental security concepts. \n\n- Confidentiality, Integrity, and Availability form the CIA triad. \n\n- Authentication verifies identity. \n\n- Authorization determines permissions. \n\n- Strong passwords and MFA improve security. \n\n- Encryption protects confidential information. \n\n- Symmetric and asymmetric cryptography use different key models. \n\n- Hash functions support integrity verification. \n\n- Digital signatures provide authenticity and integrity. \n\n- Malware includes viruses, worms, trojans, and ransomware. \n\n- Social engineering attacks people rather than technology. \n\n- Phishing is one of the most common cyber threats. \n\n- Good security practices significantly reduce risk. ","resultHTML":"<section data-type=\"sect1\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture09-c3515-summary\">\n<h1>Summary</h1>\n<p>In this chapter we learned:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Cybersecurity protects systems, data, and services.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Assets, threats, vulnerabilities, and risks are fundamental security concepts.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Confidentiality, Integrity, and Availability form the CIA triad.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Authentication verifies identity.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Authorization determines permissions.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Strong passwords and MFA improve security.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Encryption protects confidential information.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Symmetric and asymmetric cryptography use different key models.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Hash functions support integrity verification.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Digital signatures provide authenticity and integrity.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Malware includes viruses, worms, trojans, and ransomware.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Social engineering attacks people rather than technology.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Phishing is one of the most common cyber threats.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Good security practices significantly reduce risk.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</section>\n","hidden":true,"type":"markdown","translations":{"Dutch":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"48de42ef16fc2da62a845b33d5e4046cbf37452f5601c7cfd68d70066abaa930","markdown":"## Samenvatting\n\nIn dit hoofdstuk hebben we het volgende geleerd:\n\n- Cybersecurity beschermt systemen, gegevens en diensten.\n\n- Bezittingen, bedreigingen, kwetsbaarheden en risico's zijn fundamentele beveiligingsconcepten.\n\n- Vertrouwelijkheid, Integriteit en Beschikbaarheid vormen de CIA-triade.\n\n- Authenticatie verifieert identiteit.\n\n- Autorisatie bepaalt rechten.\n\n- Sterke wachtwoorden en MFA verbeteren de beveiliging.\n\n- Encryptie beschermt vertrouwelijke informatie.\n\n- Symmetrische en asymmetrische cryptografie gebruiken verschillende sleutelmodellen.\n\n- Hashfuncties ondersteunen integriteitsverificatie.\n\n- Digitale handtekeningen bieden authenticiteit en integriteit.\n\n- Malware omvat virussen, wormen, Trojaanse paarden en ransomware.\n\n- Social engineering valt mensen aan in plaats van technologie.\n\n- Phishing is een van de meest voorkomende cyberdreigingen.\n\n- Goede beveiligingspraktijken verminderen het risico aanzienlijk."},"French":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"48de42ef16fc2da62a845b33d5e4046cbf37452f5601c7cfd68d70066abaa930","markdown":"## Résumé\n\nDans ce chapitre, nous avons appris :\n\n- La cybersécurité protège les systèmes, les données et les services.\n\n- Les actifs, les menaces, les vulnérabilités et les risques sont des concepts de sécurité fondamentaux.\n\n- La confidentialité, l'intégrité et la disponibilité forment la triade CIA.\n\n- L'authentification vérifie l'identité.\n\n- L'autorisation détermine les permissions.\n\n- Des mots de passe forts et l'authentification multifacteur (MFA) améliorent la sécurité.\n\n- Le chiffrement protège les informations confidentielles.\n\n- La cryptographie symétrique et asymétrique utilisent des modèles de clés différents.\n\n- Les fonctions de hachage prennent en charge la vérification de l'intégrité.\n\n- Les signatures numériques assurent l'authenticité et l'intégrité.\n\n- Les logiciels malveillants comprennent les virus, les vers, les chevaux de Troie et les rançongiciels.\n\n- L'ingénierie sociale attaque les personnes plutôt que la technologie.\n\n- L'hameçonnage (phishing) est l'une des cybermenaces les plus courantes.\n\n- De bonnes pratiques de sécurité réduisent considérablement les risques."}},"translationSource":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"48de42ef16fc2da62a845b33d5e4046cbf37452f5601c7cfd68d70066abaa930","language":"English"}},{"input":"## Key Terms\n\n{.wide}\n| Term                        | Definition                                               |\n| ------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| Cybersecurity               | Protection of systems, networks, and data                    |\n| Asset                       | Valuable item requiring protection                           |\n| Threat                      | Potential source of harm                                     |\n| Vulnerability               | Weakness that can be exploited                               |\n| Risk                        | Possibility of harm resulting from a threat exploiting a vulnerability |\n| Confidentiality             | Protection against unauthorized disclosure                   |\n| Integrity                   | Protection against unauthorized modification                 |\n| Availability                | Ensuring information and systems remain accessible           |\n| Authentication              | Verification of identity                                     |\n| Authorization               | Determination of permissions                                 |\n| Encryption                  | Conversion of readable data into protected form              |\n| Key                         | Secret information used in cryptography                      |\n| Symmetric Encryption        | Encryption using one shared key                              |\n| Asymmetric Encryption       | Encryption using a public/private key pair                   |\n| Hash Function               | Function producing a fixed-size digest                       |\n| Digital Signature           | Mechanism verifying authenticity and integrity               |\n| Malware                     | Malicious software                                           |\n| Phishing                    | Fraudulent attempt to obtain sensitive information           |\n| Multi-Factor Authentication | Authentication using multiple factors                        |","output":"","result":"## Key Terms\n\n{.wide}\n| Term                        | Definition                                               |\n| ------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| Cybersecurity               | Protection of systems, networks, and data                    |\n| Asset                       | Valuable item requiring protection                           |\n| Threat                      | Potential source of harm                                     |\n| Vulnerability               | Weakness that can be exploited                               |\n| Risk                        | Possibility of harm resulting from a threat exploiting a vulnerability |\n| Confidentiality             | Protection against unauthorized disclosure                   |\n| Integrity                   | Protection against unauthorized modification                 |\n| Availability                | Ensuring information and systems remain accessible           |\n| Authentication              | Verification of identity                                     |\n| Authorization               | Determination of permissions                                 |\n| Encryption                  | Conversion of readable data into protected form              |\n| Key                         | Secret information used in cryptography                      |\n| Symmetric Encryption        | Encryption using one shared key                              |\n| Asymmetric Encryption       | Encryption using a public/private key pair                   |\n| Hash Function               | Function producing a fixed-size digest                       |\n| Digital Signature           | Mechanism verifying authenticity and integrity               |\n| Malware                     | Malicious software                                           |\n| Phishing                    | Fraudulent attempt to obtain sensitive information           |\n| Multi-Factor Authentication | Authentication using multiple factors                        |","resultHTML":"<section data-type=\"sect1\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture09-c3516-key-terms\">\n<h1>Key Terms</h1>\n<figure data-type=\"table\" class=\"wide\">\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Term</th>\n<th>Definition</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Cybersecurity</td>\n<td>Protection of systems, networks, and data</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Asset</td>\n<td>Valuable item requiring protection</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Threat</td>\n<td>Potential source of harm</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Vulnerability</td>\n<td>Weakness that can be exploited</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Risk</td>\n<td>Possibility of harm resulting from a threat exploiting a vulnerability</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Confidentiality</td>\n<td>Protection against unauthorized disclosure</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Integrity</td>\n<td>Protection against unauthorized modification</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Availability</td>\n<td>Ensuring information and systems remain accessible</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Authentication</td>\n<td>Verification of identity</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Authorization</td>\n<td>Determination of permissions</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Encryption</td>\n<td>Conversion of readable data into protected form</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Key</td>\n<td>Secret information used in cryptography</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Symmetric Encryption</td>\n<td>Encryption using one shared key</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Asymmetric Encryption</td>\n<td>Encryption using a public/private key pair</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Hash Function</td>\n<td>Function producing a fixed-size digest</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Digital Signature</td>\n<td>Mechanism verifying authenticity and integrity</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Malware</td>\n<td>Malicious software</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Phishing</td>\n<td>Fraudulent attempt to obtain sensitive information</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Multi-Factor Authentication</td>\n<td>Authentication using multiple factors</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n</figure>\n</section>\n","hidden":true,"type":"markdown","translations":{"Dutch":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"653bf691eb424d1161771f9b7b379480a00cd754ab1493f5e149fcc0a8990905","markdown":"## Kernbegrippen\n\n{.wide}\n| Term                        | Definitie                                               |\n| ------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| Cybersecurity               | Bescherming van systemen, netwerken en gegevens               |\n| Asset                       | Waardevol item dat bescherming vereist                       |\n| Threat                      | Mogelijke bron van schade                                    |\n| Vulnerability               | Zwakte die kan worden misbruikt                              |\n| Risk                        | Mogelijkheid van schade als gevolg van een dreiging die een kwetsbaarheid misbruikt |\n| Confidentiality             | Bescherming tegen ongeoorloofde openbaarmaking                |\n| Integrity                   | Bescherming tegen ongeoorloofde wijziging                     |\n| Availability                | Zorgen dat informatie en systemen toegankelijk blijven        |\n| Authentication              | Verificatie van identiteit                                   |\n| Authorization               | Bepaling van machtigingen                                    |\n| Encryption                  | Omzetting van leesbare gegevens naar beschermde vorm           |\n| Key                         | Geheime informatie gebruikt in cryptografie                   |\n| Symmetric Encryption        | Versleuteling met één gedeelde sleutel                        |\n| Asymmetric Encryption       | Versleuteling met een publiek/privaat sleutelpaar             |\n| Hash Function               | Functie die een samenvatting van vaste grootte produceert     |\n| Digital Signature           | Mechanisme dat authenticiteit en integriteit verifieert        |\n| Malware                     | Kwaadaardige software                                         |\n| Phishing                    | Frauduleuze poging om gevoelige informatie te verkrijgen       |\n| Multi-Factor Authentication | Authenticatie met meerdere factoren                           |"},"French":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"653bf691eb424d1161771f9b7b379480a00cd754ab1493f5e149fcc0a8990905","markdown":"## Termes clés\n\n{.wide}\n| Terme                        | Définition                                               |\n| ------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| Cybersécurité               | Protection des systèmes, des réseaux et des données           |\n| Actif                       | Élément de valeur nécessitant une protection                 |\n| Menace                      | Source potentielle de préjudice                              |\n| Vulnérabilité               | Faiblesse pouvant être exploitée                              |\n| Risque                      | Possibilité de préjudice résultant de l'exploitation d'une vulnérabilité par une menace |\n| Confidentialité             | Protection contre la divulgation non autorisée               |\n| Intégrité                   | Protection contre la modification non autorisée              |\n| Disponibilité               | Garantie que les informations et les systèmes restent accessibles |\n| Authentification            | Vérification de l'identité                                   |\n| Autorisation                | Détermination des permissions                                 |\n| Chiffrement                 | Conversion de données lisibles en une forme protégée          |\n| Clé                         | Information secrète utilisée en cryptographie                 |\n| Chiffrement symétrique      | Chiffrement utilisant une clé partagée unique                 |\n| Chiffrement asymétrique     | Chiffrement utilisant une paire de clés publique/privée       |\n| Fonction de hachage         | Fonction produisant un condensé de taille fixe                |\n| Signature numérique         | Mécanisme vérifiant l'authenticité et l'intégrité             |\n| Logiciel malveillant        | Logiciel malveillant                                          |\n| Hameçonnage                 | Tentative frauduleuse d'obtenir des informations sensibles    |\n| Authentification multifacteur | Authentification utilisant plusieurs facteurs               |"}},"translationSource":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"653bf691eb424d1161771f9b7b379480a00cd754ab1493f5e149fcc0a8990905","language":"English"}},{"input":"## Review Questions \n\n- What is cybersecurity? \n\n- What is the difference between an asset, a threat, and a vulnerability? \n\n- Explain the CIA triad. \n\n- What is the difference between authentication and authorization? \n\n- Why are strong passwords important? \n\n- What is multi-factor authentication? \n\n- What problem does encryption solve? \n\n- What is the difference between symmetric and asymmetric encryption? \n\n- What is the purpose of a hash function? \n\n- Why are digital signatures useful? \n\n- What is malware? \n\n- How does a ransomware attack work? \n\n- What is social engineering? \n\n- How can phishing attacks be recognized? \n\n- Which security practices should every user follow? ","output":"","result":"## Review Questions \n\n- What is cybersecurity? \n\n- What is the difference between an asset, a threat, and a vulnerability? \n\n- Explain the CIA triad. \n\n- What is the difference between authentication and authorization? \n\n- Why are strong passwords important? \n\n- What is multi-factor authentication? \n\n- What problem does encryption solve? \n\n- What is the difference between symmetric and asymmetric encryption? \n\n- What is the purpose of a hash function? \n\n- Why are digital signatures useful? \n\n- What is malware? \n\n- How does a ransomware attack work? \n\n- What is social engineering? \n\n- How can phishing attacks be recognized? \n\n- Which security practices should every user follow? ","resultHTML":"<section data-type=\"sect1\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture09-c3517-review-questions\">\n<h1>Review Questions</h1>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>What is cybersecurity?</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>What is the difference between an asset, a threat, and a vulnerability?</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Explain the CIA triad.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>What is the difference between authentication and authorization?</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Why are strong passwords important?</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>What is multi-factor authentication?</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>What problem does encryption solve?</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>What is the difference between symmetric and asymmetric encryption?</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>What is the purpose of a hash function?</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Why are digital signatures useful?</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>What is malware?</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>How does a ransomware attack work?</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>What is social engineering?</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>How can phishing attacks be recognized?</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Which security practices should every user follow?</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</section>\n","hidden":true,"type":"markdown","translations":{"Dutch":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"fc630c6a8aab41421c3e54603b6248d13b8042271f3615e893d88401a262faf5","markdown":"## Vragen ter herhaling\n\n- Wat is cybersecurity?\n\n- Wat is het verschil tussen een asset, een dreiging en een kwetsbaarheid?\n\n- Leg de CIA-triade uit.\n\n- Wat is het verschil tussen authenticatie en autorisatie?\n\n- Waarom zijn sterke wachtwoorden belangrijk?\n\n- Wat is meerfactorauthenticatie?\n\n- Welk probleem lost versleuteling op?\n\n- Wat is het verschil tussen symmetrische en asymmetrische versleuteling?\n\n- Wat is het doel van een hashfunctie?\n\n- Waarom zijn digitale handtekeningen nuttig?\n\n- Wat is malware?\n\n- Hoe werkt een ransomware-aanval?\n\n- Wat is social engineering?\n\n- Hoe kunnen phishingaanvallen herkend worden?\n\n- Welke beveiligingspraktijken moet elke gebruiker volgen?"},"French":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"fc630c6a8aab41421c3e54603b6248d13b8042271f3615e893d88401a262faf5","markdown":"## Questions de révision\n\n- Qu'est-ce que la cybersécurité ?\n\n- Quelle est la différence entre un actif, une menace et une vulnérabilité ?\n\n- Expliquez la triade CIA.\n\n- Quelle est la différence entre l'authentification et l'autorisation ?\n\n- Pourquoi les mots de passe forts sont-ils importants ?\n\n- Qu'est-ce que l'authentification multifacteur ?\n\n- Quel problème le chiffrement résout-il ?\n\n- Quelle est la différence entre le chiffrement symétrique et asymétrique ?\n\n- Quel est le but d'une fonction de hachage ?\n\n- Pourquoi les signatures numériques sont-elles utiles ?\n\n- Qu'est-ce qu'un logiciel malveillant ?\n\n- Comment fonctionne une attaque par rançongiciel ?\n\n- Qu'est-ce que l'ingénierie sociale ?\n\n- Comment peut-on reconnaître les attaques par hameçonnage ?\n\n- Quelles pratiques de sécurité chaque utilisateur devrait-il suivre ?"}},"translationSource":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"fc630c6a8aab41421c3e54603b6248d13b8042271f3615e893d88401a262faf5","language":"English"}},{"input":"## Transition to Lecture 10 \n\nThroughout this course, we have studied how computers represent information, execute software, communicate through networks, and protect data. One of the most important recent developments in computing is the rise of **Artificial Intelligence**, particularly systems capable of generating text, images, audio, and software. \n\nIn the final leture, we will explore **Generative Artificial Intelligence**, how it works, its capabilities, its limitations, and its growing role in modern society. ","output":"","result":"## Transition to Lecture 10 \n\nThroughout this course, we have studied how computers represent information, execute software, communicate through networks, and protect data. One of the most important recent developments in computing is the rise of **Artificial Intelligence**, particularly systems capable of generating text, images, audio, and software. \n\nIn the final leture, we will explore **Generative Artificial Intelligence**, how it works, its capabilities, its limitations, and its growing role in modern society. ","resultHTML":"<section data-type=\"sect1\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture09-c3518-transition-to-lecture-10\">\n<h1>Transition to Lecture 10</h1>\n<p>Throughout this course, we have studied how computers represent information, execute software, communicate through networks, and protect data. One of the most important recent developments in computing is the rise of <strong>Artificial Intelligence</strong>, particularly systems capable of generating text, images, audio, and software.</p>\n<p>In the final leture, we will explore <strong>Generative Artificial Intelligence</strong>, how it works, its capabilities, its limitations, and its growing role in modern society.</p>\n</section>\n","hidden":true,"type":"markdown","translations":{"Dutch":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"bf5c83c746518341dc1ecc51e29e43aa42e7dd95b659cda5a0cfbe3e0cb47ae4","markdown":"## Overgang naar Les 10\n\nGedurende deze cursus hebben we bestudeerd hoe computers informatie voorstellen, software uitvoeren, communiceren via netwerken en gegevens beschermen. Een van de belangrijkste recente ontwikkelingen in de informatica is de opkomst van **kunstmatige intelligentie**, in het bijzonder systemen die in staat zijn tekst, beelden, audio en software te genereren.\n\nIn de laatste les verkennen we **generatieve kunstmatige intelligentie**: hoe ze werkt, haar mogelijkheden, haar beperkingen en haar groeiende rol in de moderne samenleving."},"French":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"bf5c83c746518341dc1ecc51e29e43aa42e7dd95b659cda5a0cfbe3e0cb47ae4","markdown":"## Transition vers le cours 10\n\nTout au long de ce cours, nous avons étudié comment les ordinateurs représentent l'information, exécutent des logiciels, communiquent via des réseaux et protègent les données. L'un des développements récents les plus importants en informatique est l'essor de l'**intelligence artificielle**, en particulier des systèmes capables de générer du texte, des images, de l'audio et des logiciels.\n\nDans le dernier cours, nous explorerons l'**intelligence artificielle générative**, son fonctionnement, ses capacités, ses limites et son rôle croissant dans la société moderne."}},"translationSource":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"bf5c83c746518341dc1ecc51e29e43aa42e7dd95b659cda5a0cfbe3e0cb47ae4","language":"English"}}]